# Resource Groups Tagging API Tagging API Reference

> The AWS services in the following list support the Resource Groups Tagging API TagResources and UntagResources operations.

- [Welcome](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/Welcome.md)
- [Common Parameters](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/CommonParameters.md)
- [Common Error Types](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/CommonErrors.md)

## [Actions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/API_Operations.md)

- [DescribeReportCreation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/API_DescribeReportCreation.md): Describes the status of the StartReportCreation operation.
- [GetComplianceSummary](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/API_GetComplianceSummary.md): Returns a table that shows counts of resources that are noncompliant with their tag policies.
- [GetResources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/API_GetResources.md): Returns all the tagged or previously tagged resources that are located in the specified AWS Region for the account.
- [GetTagKeys](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/API_GetTagKeys.md): Returns all tag keys currently in use in the specified AWS Region for the calling account.
- [GetTagValues](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/API_GetTagValues.md): Returns all tag values for the specified key that are used in the specified AWS Region for the calling account.
- [ListRequiredTags](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/API_ListRequiredTags.md): Lists the required tags for supported resource types in an AWS account.
- [StartReportCreation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/API_StartReportCreation.md): Generates a report that lists all tagged resources in the accounts across your organization and tells whether each resource is compliant with the effective tag policy.
- [TagResources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/API_TagResources.md): Applies one or more tags to the specified resources.
- [UntagResources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/API_UntagResources.md): Removes the specified tags from the specified resources.


## [Data Types](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/API_Types.md)

- [ComplianceDetails](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/API_ComplianceDetails.md): Information that shows whether a resource is compliant with the effective tag policy, including details on any noncompliant tag keys.
- [FailureInfo](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/API_FailureInfo.md): Information about the errors that are returned for each failed resource.
- [RequiredTag](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/API_RequiredTag.md): Information that describes the required tags for a given resource type.
- [ResourceTagMapping](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/API_ResourceTagMapping.md): A list of resource ARNs and the tags (keys and values) that are associated with each.
- [Summary](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/API_Summary.md): A count of noncompliant resources.
- [Tag](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/API_Tag.md): The metadata that you apply to AWS resources to help you categorize and organize them.
- [TagFilter](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/API_TagFilter.md): A list of tags (keys and values) that are used to specify the associated resources.


